WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.128
I wanted to show how I would approach a core business applications problem: reducing manual operational work without removing human judgement.

2
00:00:09.328 --> 00:00:20.867
Instead of an employee manually reading a submission, entering the data, checking for duplicates, and deciding where it goes, I built a workflow that handles the repeatable parts automatically.

3
00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:30.724
The important part was not just adding AI. I designed the data model, business rules, exception paths, and human-review logic around it.

4
00:00:31.924 --> 00:00:40.769
Azure Document Intelligence extracts policy data. Dataverse structures the client and submission records.

5
00:00:40.769 --> 00:00:52.899
The workflow checks existing records, flags possible duplicates, applies deterministic routing rules, and sends uncertain cases to human review.

6
00:00:54.099 --> 00:01:05.145
I also documented the current and future process, functional requirements, acceptance criteria, and test cases so the system could be maintained and improved.

7
00:01:06.345 --> 00:01:18.520
The result is a working example of how I approach business applications: understand the process, structure the data, automate what is repeatable, and keep people involved where judgement is required.
